                <pb facs="0465" n="455" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv10/pg455"/>

                <head>Appendix 236</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#italic">Analyses of Contributions of the
                        Various Countries Towards Relief From 1st December, 1918, to 31st May,
                        1919</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Herbert Hoover</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Director-General of Relief.</hi></p>
                <p>At your request I have formulated the following analyses of the respective
                    contributions of the various countries towards relief during the period from the
                    1st December, 1918, to the 31st May, 1919.</p>
                <p>The first three tables give respectively summaries of:— <list>
                        <item>Total delivered by each country (Table I).</item>
                        <item>Proportion furnished on credit and for cash (Table II).</item>
                        <item>Origin of the tonnage (Table III).</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The detailed tables give the deliveries to each of the relief countries during
                    this period by:— <list>
                        <item>United States (Table IV).</item>
                        <item>United Kingdom (Table V).</item>
                        <item>France (Table VI).</item>
                        <item>Italy (Table VII).</item>
                        <pb facs="0466" n="456" xml:id="pg456"/>
                        <item>Joint Allied Finance (Table VIII).</item>
                        <item>All other countries (Table IX).</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank M. Surface</hi></signed><lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Chief, Statistical Division</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">American Relief Administration.</hi></closer>
